  CAPACITY IS NOT WHAT THIS MEASURES. At k=9 the creature meets its own
  geometry on both axes: per-axis accuracy is within 2 SE of what the
  DELIVERED spacing and the within-level scatter predict. The fall from
  k=4's +0.137 is resolution, not vocabulary -- the span is pinned at the
  learned reach and nine words subdivide it until adjacent levels sit
  inside the creature's own scatter. NO vocabulary limit is shown. The
  binding constraint is reach / scatter, and it is the REACH that must
  grow: ctxscale's ~118 Hz asymptote already holds only ~2 levels per
  axis, which is exactly the 2x2 that ctxgrid found working.
